            "rationale": "The requirement defines 'on shelf' as 'not on loan'. The change derives that status inside the Tier 3 view code by testing the loan map. It does not ask a Tier 1/2 function. The change adds no new guard, transition or invariant, and the Tier 3 derivation agrees with the stated rule. Search matching (title or author, ignoring case) is projection logic and is acceptable in Tier 3. The status derivation is the only domain rule sitting outside Tier 1/2, so this is a partial deviation rather than a contradiction. I could not see whether Tier 2 already has an on-loan predicate; if it does, this should have called it.",
